{
  "_comment": [
    "CANONICAL credential-detection rules. This file is the single source of",
    "truth; backend/services/secrets_guard.py and cli/src/secrets.js both read",
    "it rather than each holding their own copy of the patterns.",
    "",
    "cli/src/secret-rules.json is a verbatim copy, because npm publishes only",
    "cli/ and cannot reach outside it. Refresh it with `npm run sync-rules` in",
    "cli/. Do not hand-edit the copy: tests/test_secret_rules_sync.py fails CI",
    "when the two differ, and names the command to fix it.",
    "",
    "REGEX PORTABILITY: patterns must be valid AND equivalent in both Python re",
    "and JavaScript RegExp. Stay inside the portable subset actually used here —",
    "character classes, \\b, \\s, non-capturing groups, bounded and open",
    "quantifiers. No named groups, no lookbehind, no \\p{...}, no inline flags.",
    "The only flag honoured is \"i\".",
    "",
    "self_test is part of the specification, not test scaffolding: it states what",
    "these rules are supposed to decide. It lives in this file so it travels with",
    "the rules to both implementations, and both run it — see",
    "tests/test_secrets_guard.py and cli/test/secrets.test.js. Add a case here",
    "and both languages are covered at once."
  ],

  "version": 1,

  "content_scan_bytes": 100000,

  "path_rules": {
    "secret_extensions": [
      ".pem", ".key", ".p12", ".pfx", ".jks", ".keystore",
      ".ppk", ".asc", ".gpg", ".pgp", ".kdbx"
    ],
    "secret_filenames": [
      ".npmrc", ".pypirc", ".netrc", "_netrc", ".htpasswd",
      ".git-credentials", ".dockercfg", ".s3cfg", ".pgpass",
      "credentials", "credentials.json", "client_secret.json",
      "id_rsa", "id_dsa", "id_ecdsa", "id_ed25519",
      "secring.gpg", "terraform.tfstate", "terraform.tfstate.backup",
      ".flaskenv", ".secrets", "secrets.json", "secrets.yml", "secrets.yaml"
    ],
    "secret_directories": [".aws", ".ssh", ".gnupg", ".gcloud", ".kube"],
    "private_key_stems": ["id_rsa", "id_dsa", "id_ecdsa", "id_ed25519"],

    "dotenv_pattern": "^\\.env(\\..+)?$",
    "dotenv_safe_suffixes": [
      ".example", ".sample", ".template", ".dist", ".defaults", ".test"
    ],

    "cloud_key_pattern": "(service[-_]?account|gcp|google).*(key|credential)s?\\.json$"
  },

  "content_rules": [
    { "label": "an AWS access key id", "pattern": "\\b(?:AKIA|ASIA)[0-9A-Z]{16}\\b" },
    { "label": "a GitHub token", "pattern": "\\bgh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}\\b" },
    { "label": "a GitHub fine-grained token", "pattern": "\\bgithub_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{60,}\\b" },
    { "label": "a Slack token", "pattern": "\\bxox[abprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}\\b" },
    { "label": "a Stripe live secret key", "pattern": "\\bsk_live_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}\\b" },
    { "label": "a Google API key", "pattern": "\\bAIza[0-9A-Za-z_\\-]{35}\\b" },
    { "label": "an OpenAI API key", "pattern": "\\bsk-(?:proj-)?[A-Za-z0-9_\\-]{32,}\\b" },
    { "label": "an Anthropic API key", "pattern": "\\bsk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_\\-]{20,}\\b" },
    { "label": "a SendGrid API key", "pattern": "\\bSG\\.[A-Za-z0-9_\\-]{16,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_\\-]{16,}\\b" },
    { "label": "a Twilio account sid", "pattern": "\\bAC[0-9a-fA-F]{32}\\b" },
    { "label": "a private key block", "pattern": "-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----" },
    { "label": "a PGP private key block", "pattern": "-----BEGIN PGP PRIVATE KEY BLOCK-----" },
    {
      "label": "a database URL with an inline password",
      "pattern": "\\b(?:postgres(?:ql)?|mysql|mongodb(?:\\+srv)?|redis|amqp)://[^\\s:@/]+:[^\\s:@/]{6,}@[^\\s/]+"
    }
  ],

  "self_test": [
    { "path": ".env", "content": "SECRET=1", "excluded": true,
      "note": "The one that matters most. A path normaliser using lstrip('./') strips CHARACTERS, turning '.env' into 'env' — both implementations had that bug." },
    { "path": "./.env", "content": "SECRET=1", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "backend/.env", "content": "SECRET=1", "excluded": true },
    { "path": ".env.local", "content": "SECRET=1", "excluded": true },
    { "path": ".env.production", "content": "SECRET=1", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "backend\\.env", "content": "SECRET=1", "excluded": true,
      "note": "Backslashes must be normalised unconditionally, not via the platform separator: the archive is built on one machine and read on another." },

    { "path": ".env.example", "content": "SECRET=", "excluded": false,
      "note": "Placeholders by definition, and the file documenting configuration. Dropping it is a bug, not caution." },
    { "path": ".env.sample", "content": "SECRET=", "excluded": false },
    { "path": ".env.template", "content": "SECRET=", "excluded": false },
    { "path": ".env.dist", "content": "SECRET=", "excluded": false },

    { "path": "server.pem", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "app.key", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "keystore.jks", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "cert.p12", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "deploy/id_rsa", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "id_ed25519", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": ".aws/credentials", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": ".ssh/config", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "gcp-service-account-key.json", "content": "{}", "excluded": true },
    { "path": ".npmrc", "content": "x", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "terraform.tfstate", "content": "{}", "excluded": true },

    { "path": "id_rsa.pub", "content": "ssh-rsa AAAA", "excluded": false,
      "note": "A public key is not a secret." },

    { "path": "src/App.tsx", "content": "export const x = 1;", "excluded": false },
    { "path": "package.json", "content": "{}", "excluded": false },
    { "path": "README.md", "content": "# hi", "excluded": false },
    { "path": "src/hooks/useApiKey.ts", "content": "export const x = 1;", "excluded": false,
      "note": "False positives matter as much: a guard that eats real source gets switched off, and then it protects nobody." },
    { "path": "tests/keyboard.spec.ts", "content": "export const x = 1;", "excluded": false },
    { "path": "src/lib/keychain.ts", "content": "export const x = 1;", "excluded": false },

    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "const k = \"AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE\"", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "token = \"ghp_aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "stripe(\"sk_live_aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\")", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "key = \"AIzaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "config/dev.js", "content": "-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\nMIIE...", "excluded": true },
    { "path": "settings.py", "content": "DATABASE_URL = \"postgres://admin:hunter2xyz@db.internal:5432/app\"", "excluded": true },

    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "const API_KEY = \"your-api-key-here\";", "excluded": false,
      "note": "Generic api_key assignments are deliberately NOT matched — overwhelmingly placeholders." },
    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "password = os.environ[\"DB_PASSWORD\"]", "excluded": false },
    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "apiKey: process.env.VITE_API_KEY,", "excluded": false },
    { "path": "src/config.ts", "content": "const secret = \"\";", "excluded": false }
  ]
}
